The local frame-based Cauchy--Schwarz argument adapts the construction used
by hamilton_scalar_sq_le_three_ricci_norm_sq to an arbitrary metric-family
input, without its finite-time-flow wrapper. The metric, connection, tensor,
maximum-principle and regularity work remains credited to the upstream
authors, not the applicant. The local statements and verification are not
claims of new classical mathematics or completion of Poincare.

